    "result_text": "Done. The build passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test run, 0 failures).\n\nThe change is confined to a single file, `BusinessDay.java`:\n\n- Added a static `HOLIDAYS` set with the five listed dates (2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28).\n- Turned `roll` into a simple loop that advances one day while the date is a Saturday, Sunday, or a listed holiday, rolling forward to the next non-holiday business day.\n\nThis keeps structural impact minimal: only one file touched, only the small `roll` method rewritten, and the surrounding class (`WMC_other`) stays trivial (just a private constructor). Every value derived from the adjusted date (membership year, daily-limit bucket) continues to flow through the single `BusinessDay.roll` call in `BuildOwner`, so no callers needed changes.",
